# How to cite LIBs. GitHub reads this file and shows a "Cite this repository"
# button on the repository page (APA and BibTeX, ready to copy).
# After Zenodo gives LIBs a DOI, uncomment the `doi:` line and paste it in.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If LIBs helps your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LIBs: battery analysis software"
abstract: >-
  Free, open-source software that turns raw battery cycler and potentiostat
  files (NEWARE, WonATech, BioLogic, IVIUM, ESPEC) into publication-ready
  figures, a table of numbers and written findings, without coding. It covers
  GCD/CE, cycling, rate, dQ/dV, EIS, DRT, XPS, CV, FTIR, SEM, GITT and Tafel,
  and scales to hundreds of cells and public datasets.
authors:
  - family-names: Mpupuni
    given-names: Carlos Tafara
    affiliation: Chungnam National University
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
version: 1.0.0
# date-released: 2026-11-20
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.0000000
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/carlostafarampupuni/LIBs"
keywords:
  - battery
  - electrochemistry
  - lithium-ion
  - impedance spectroscopy
  - data analysis
